I like the DS port, but I found it frustrating trying to move
diagonally.  I ended up using the stylus for movement all the time,
but you should be able to lock into diagonal movement by holding R or
something (the author mentions that this may be in a future release,
but who knows when that will be).

It's a great port though, the programmable hotkeys and quick menu with
all the commands work really well.  But do you find that you often get
the same few roles chosen for you, or you seem to find certain rare
items a lot?  I haven't played on the DS in a while, but mine seemed
to have an affinity for Fire Horns...

And yeah, it's not commercial, the only catch is that you have to own
a Nintendo DS, buy special hardware and configure it yourself to be
able to play it. :p


